Z||000004||Leadfoot||08-14-2001||04:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GML:<BR><B>I recently had my fuel injection system cleaned and when I picked up the car it was idleing around 2000rpm.  I replaced the IAC sensor which brought it down to around 1500rpm, but I'm still not happy with it.  Any ideas?????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you replaced the IAC you have to warm up the car and drive it past 35mph so it can reset.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GML||08-14-2001||04:35 PM||||I did that and it did drop it down to about 1500rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kiteman||08-15-2001||09:37 PM||||I had a high idle around 1500 rpm when my TPS was beginning to fail.  It wouldn't light up my Check Engine light so I couldn't get any diagnostic code readout.  This went on for about a week and drove me nuts trying to figure out the cause.  Finally it failed enough to get a code. I replaced it, and the idle returned to normal.||||reg||1
Z||000007||btoth||08-15-2001||10:42 PM||||V6 or 4cyl?<P>Try resetting the computer.  Unplug the battery for a while (I forgot how long, 5 min??)... then try driving the car and see if you set any trouble codes.  <P>There is a way to adjust the idle on the V6, I don't know how.  But you shouldn't have to mess with that.<P>When at normal operating temp, mine idles at 800 RPM in drive.  About 1000 RPM in park.||||reg||1
